For the SSP2-EM and SSP5-EM simulations, we held historical population constant while using scenario-specific projections (SSP2-4.5 and SSP5-8.5) for fire carbon emissions, burned area, and PM₂.₅ concentrations. These data were shared previously and are not duplicated here.

pop_0.1x0.1_2010.npz
Gridded population data (ages 25+) were derived from the GPWv4.11 Basic Demographic Characteristics dataset. The original 2.5 arc-minute data were aggregated to a 0.1° × 0.1° resolution. Units remain consistent with the source (counts per grid cell).

SSP245-EM_mortality.csv and SSP585-EM_mortality.csv
Contain global gridded fire-induced PM₂.₅-related mortality at 0.1° × 0.1° resolution, reported as thousands of deaths per grid cell, averaged over 2095–2099 under the SSP2-4.5 and SSP5-8.5 scenarios.